fortibackup (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(watchdog): backup-overdue detection. A new optional [watchdog]
    block enables a background task that periodically checks each device's
    last *successful* backup time and alerts (over notifications.on_failure
    channels) when one goes stale. This catches the silent failure case a
    failed-fetch alert can't: scheduler stopped, host went down, device
    became unreachable for longer than expected — no fetch was attempted,
    so nothing "failed".
  * storage: a `.last_success` dotfile is written under each device's
    directory on every successful run, including no_change runs. The
    watchdog reads this marker rather than the newest file's mtime,
    because under dedup the newest file can be days old even while
    backups keep succeeding — measuring against it would produce a daily
    false alarm. The dotfile is invisible to listings and retention.
  * notify: two new statuses — Stale and Recovered. Both ride the
    on_failure channels: stale fires once on threshold crossing, re-fires
    at most every 24h while the device remains stale, and a one-shot
    recovery notice is sent when backups resume.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Mon, 01 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(webui): decode `+` as space in form-urlencoded POST bodies. The
    /config save handler treated `+` literally instead of as a space (the
    encoding browsers use for spaces in application/x-www-form-urlencoded),
    which made every save fail TOML validation with errors like
    `backup_dir+=+"/var/lib/fortibackup"`. Path segments still treat `+`
    literally — only form fields convert. Caught on first real save attempt.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Mon, 25 May 2026 21:50:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(webui): live config editor with hot reload. New page at /config
    shows the current /etc/fortibackup/config.toml in a textarea; saving
    parses + validates the new TOML, backs up the previous file as
    config.toml.bak-<unix>, writes the new one, and sends a reload event
    to the scheduler — which tears down all current jobs and installs
    the new ones in-process. Zero restart, no missed cron wakeups beyond
    the few-millisecond swap.
  * scheduler: now loops on an mpsc Receiver<Config> in addition to the
    shutdown signal; rebuilds jobs on every received config. The shared
    Arc<Config> is swapped atomically before tear-down so any backup that
    fires *during* the swap reads consistent data.
  * systemd: ReadWritePaths now includes /etc/fortibackup so the daemon
    can rewrite config.toml under ProtectSystem=strict.
  * chore(msrv): bump rust-version from 1.75 to 1.80 — unblocks
    dependabot updates that already moved past 1.75.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Mon, 25 May 2026 21:30:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(webui): diff between two arbitrary backups, not just consecutive
    ones. Each device page now shows a "Compare A → B" form with two
    dropdowns populated from the device's backup history. Form submits
    as `GET /diff/<device>?a=<file>&b=<file>`, the order is normalized
    chronologically (older → newer) regardless of selection direction.
    The original `/diff/<device>/<file>` shortcut still works.
    Useful for audit queries like "what changed since last month?".

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Thu, 22 May 2026 09:00:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(webui): diff view between consecutive backups. Each backup row in
    the device page now has a "diff" link that shows what changed between
    that backup and the previous one. The diff is computed over the
    normalized content (same normalization the dedup hash uses), so the
    visible output reflects real configuration changes — not the ENC
    blob re-encryption noise FortiOS introduces on every fetch.
    Built on the `similar` crate; grouped hunks with 3 lines of context,
    line-level color (green/red/gray), shrunk to the parts that actually
    changed.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Wed, 21 May 2026 08:30:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(systemd): ExecStart pointed at /usr/local/bin/fortibackup but the
    .deb installs the binary at /usr/bin/fortibackup. The service failed
    to start cleanly after a fresh `apt install` until the operator created
    a symlink. Unit now uses /usr/bin/fortibackup, matching the package.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Tue, 19 May 2026 18:40:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Embedded Web UI. New optional [webui] block enables a server-side
    rendered dashboard on the daemon: lists devices, shows backup
    history per device, allows downloading the .conf and the JSON
    sidecar, and exposes a "Run now" button that triggers a backup
    on demand. HTTP Basic auth on every endpoint; credentials are
    compared in constant time. Concurrent manual runs of the same
    device are rejected with HTTP 409 to avoid races with the
    scheduler. Path-traversal in download URLs returns HTTP 400.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Tue, 19 May 2026 18:00:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Dedup normalization: strip ENC blobs and encrypted PEM private keys
    before hashing for `no_change` detection. FortiOS re-encrypts these
    with a fresh IV on every backup fetch, which previously caused every
    run to write a new file. Validated against a live FG200F running
    FortiOS 7.2.13: identical configs now dedupe correctly.
  * Sidecar gains `raw_sha256` (hash of literal bytes) alongside the
    existing `sha256` (now the normalized dedup hash). Old sidecars
    without `raw_sha256` remain readable.
  * Status parser accepts FortiOS 7.2.13 layout (serial/version at the
    response root, not inside `results`); sidecars on this firmware now
    capture firmware_version and serial correctly.

 -- Luis Herrera <luis.herrera@rnpn.gob.sv>  Tue, 19 May 2026 17:50:00 +0000

fortibackup (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Optional VDOM scope per device (vdom = "tenant-x").
  * Post-fetch payload validation: reject HTML / login walls / truncated
    bodies that would otherwise be persisted as fake backups.
  * S3 / S3-compatible (MinIO, Wasabi, B2) mirror destination, configured
    under [storage.s3]. Filesystem remains the authoritative store.
  * Shell completions (bash/zsh/fish) and man page packaged with the .deb.

